.TH MACOSX-CROSS-CLANGD 1 "2026-09-09" "macosx-cross @MACOSX_CROSS_VERSION@" "macOS Cross Development Tools"
.SH NAME
macosx-cross-clangd \- clangd wrapper for macOS cross development
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B macosx-cross-clangd
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ clangd-options... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B macosx-cross-clangd
is a wrapper around
.BR clangd (1)
for C and C++ development targeting Apple platforms from a non-Apple host.

It selects a macOS SDK, determines the target architecture and platform,
sets the appropriate deployment target environment, and invokes
.BR clangd (1)
with the macOS cross compiler supplied by
.BR macosx-cross-clang (1).

The wrapper is intended for use with editor and language-server integrations
such as compile_commands.json based development environments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --macosx-sdk= version
Select the macOS SDK version.

If omitted, the value of
.B MACOSX_SDK_VERSION
is used. If neither is set, the default SDK root is used.

.TP
.BI --target= triple
Select the Apple target triple.

Examples include:
.BR x86_64-apple-darwin ,
.BR arm64-apple-darwin ,
and
.BR arm64-apple-ios-macabi .

.TP
.BI --arch= arch
Explicitly select the target architecture.

If omitted, the architecture is inferred from
.B --target .

Supported architectures include
.BR x86_64 ,
.BR arm64 ,
.BR arm64e ,
.BR arm ,
and
.BR i386 .

.TP
.BI --clangd= path
Use the specified
.BR clangd (1)
executable instead of automatically locating one.

.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Display usage information and exit.

.PP
All other arguments are passed directly to
.BR clangd (1).
.SH TARGET PLATFORMS
The target platform is determined from the Apple target triple.

.TP
.B *-apple-darwin*
Selects the macOS platform.

.TP
.B *-apple-ios*
Selects the iOS platform.

.TP
.B *-apple-ios-macabi*
Selects the Mac Catalyst platform.
.SH DEPLOYMENT TARGET
For macOS targets, the deployment target is obtained from
.B MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
or, if unset, from the selected SDK version.

For iOS and Mac Catalyst targets, the deployment target is obtained from
.B IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
or, if unset, from the selected SDK version.

The selected deployment target is exported before
.BR clangd (1)
is started.
.SH QUERY DRIVER
If no
.B --query-driver=
option is supplied,
.B macosx-cross-clangd
automatically adds:

.PP
.nf
--query-driver=<macosx-cross-clang>
.fi
.PP

This allows
.BR clangd (1)
to query the cross compiler for compiler-provided system include paths.

The compiler is the
.B macosx-cross-clang
wrapper selected by the installation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MACOSX_SDK_VERSION
Default SDK version.

.TP
.B MACOSX_TARGET
Default Apple target triple.

.TP
.B MACOSX_ARCH
Default target architecture.

.TP
.B MACOSX_CLANGD
Path to the
.BR clangd (1)
executable.

.TP
.B MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
Deployment target for macOS.

.TP
.B IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
Deployment target for iOS and Mac Catalyst.

.SH SDK METADATA
If the selected SDK contains a
.B .metadata
file, it is sourced before SDK and deployment information is resolved.

The metadata may provide
.B SDK_VERSION
and other SDK-specific configuration used by the macOS cross-toolchain.
.SH CLANGD SELECTION
Unless
.B MACOSX_CLANGD
or
.B --clangd=
is specified, the following executables are searched:

.PP
.nf
clangd-19
clangd
/usr/bin/clangd-19
/usr/bin/clangd
/bin/clangd-19
/bin/clangd
.fi

The first executable found is used.
.SH COMPILER SELECTION
The wrapper searches for
.B macosx-cross-clang
in the following locations:

.PP
.nf
/bin/macosx-cross-clang
/usr/bin/macosx-cross-clang
.fi

If none of these paths exists, the command is searched for using
.BR command (1).
.SH ARGUMENT PASSING
Arguments not recognized by
.B macosx-cross-clangd
are passed unchanged to
.BR clangd (1).

For example:

.PP
.nf
macosx-cross-clangd \\
    --target=x86_64-apple-darwin \\
    --compile-commands-dir=build
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Select an SDK and macOS target:
.PP
.nf
macosx-cross-clangd \\
    --macosx-sdk=10.9 \\
    --target=x86_64-apple-darwin
.fi

.TP
Use environment variables:
.PP
.nf
MACOSX_SDK_VERSION=10.9 \\
MACOSX_TARGET=x86_64-apple-darwin \\
    macosx-cross-clangd
.fi

.TP
Use an ARM64 macOS target:
.PP
.nf
macosx-cross-clangd \\
    --macosx-sdk=10.9 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-darwin
.fi

.TP
Specify a compilation database:
.PP
.nf
macosx-cross-clangd \\
    --macosx-sdk=10.9 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-darwin \\
    --compile-commands-dir=build
.fi

.TP
Use a specific clangd executable:
.PP
.nf
macosx-cross-clangd \\
    --target=x86_64-apple-darwin \\
    --clangd=/opt/llvm/bin/clangd
.fi

.SH FILES
.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk
Default macOS SDK installation root.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk/<version>
Versioned macOS SDK.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk/<version>/.metadata
SDK metadata.

.TP
.I /bin/macosx-cross-clang
Cross compiler wrapper.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution of
.BR clangd (1)
or successful display of help.

.TP
.B non-zero
An error occurred while selecting the SDK, target, compiler, clangd,
or while executing
.BR clangd (1).
.SH NOTES
The wrapper does not implement a language server itself. It configures the
cross-compilation environment and delegates all language-server processing
to
.BR clangd (1).

The
.B --query-driver
option is automatically added only when the user has not supplied a
.B --query-driver=
option.

The selected target must contain an Apple platform triple recognized by the
wrapper.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clangd (1),
.BR macosx-cross (1),
.BR macosx-cross-clang (1),
.BR macosx-cross-clang++ (1)
